{
  "duration": 64.339,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 0.34,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.839,
      "end": 1.74,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.159,
      "end": 3.179,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.779,
      "end": 4.5,
      "text": "Now, in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.92,
      "end": 9.0,
      "text": "we are given that a train of length two hundred ten meter crosses a pole in fourteen seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.559,
      "end": 10.239,
      "text": "The question is"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.779,
      "end": 13.439,
      "text": "asking us to find the speed of the train in kilometer"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.859,
      "end": 14.239,
      "text": "per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.759,
      "end": 15.219,
      "text": "Now, first,"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.599,
      "end": 17.399,
      "text": "let us understand one important concept."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.959,
      "end": 19.299,
      "text": "When a train crosses a pole,"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.819,
      "end": 22.42,
      "text": "it covers a distance equal to its own length."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.799,
      "end": 25.059,
      "text": "So distance covered is two hundred ten meter,"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.519,
      "end": 27.84,
      "text": "and time taken is fourteen seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.399,
      "end": 29.34,
      "text": "Now, we know the formula."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.879,
      "end": 32.079,
      "text": "Speed is equal to distance divided by time."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.5,
      "end": 33.379,
      "text": "Putting the values,"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.759,
      "end": 36.099,
      "text": "speed is equal to two hundred ten divided by fourteen."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.719,
      "end": 37.759,
      "text": "After simplifying this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.099,
      "end": 39.539,
      "text": "we get fifteen meter per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.0,
      "end": 45.879,
      "text": "But the question is asking for the speed in kilometer per hour, not in meter per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.299,
      "end": 57.259,
      "text": "So we must convert the unit. We know one meter per second is equal to eighteen by five kilometer per hour. So fifteen into eighteen by five is fifty-four kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.68,
      "end": 60.999,
      "text": "So the speed of the train is fifty-four kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.539,
      "end": 64.339,
      "text": "Hence, the correct answer is option C."
    }
  ],
